# What an invocation is refused before anything is read, past its words'
# parse (`cli/argv.hero`) and `check`'s own flags (`cli/check_flags.hero`),
# every refusal told at once, so a second mistake is never told only after the
# first is mended (CLAUDE.md §10; batch 32): an operand that is a directory
# where the verb reads one file (`cli/file_operand.hero`, defect 2484), a flag
# of `build` its stop cannot answer (`cli/build_stops.hero`, defect 2473), and
# a `--json` with nothing to format (`cli/json_alone.hero`, defect 2483).
# The caller exits 2 where any is told, the tool unable to run what was asked.

use cli/argv
use cli/build_stops
use cli/file_operand
use cli/json_alone

# Whether this invocation holds a refusal, each one told on stderr: the
# operand first, the thing named, then the flags.
function told(inv: argv.Invocation) -> bool
    operand = file_operand.told(inv)
    stops: bool @= false

    if inv.tag == .build_cmd
        stops @ build_stops.told(inv)
    json = json_alone.told(inv)
    return operand || stops || json
